## Validation

### Positive Test

```text
Remote network authentication
        |
        v
PowerShell execution
```

occurred on the same endpoint within the configured window.

```text
Result:
PASS
```

### Negative-Test Requirements

The correlation is designed not to trigger when:

- Only remote network authentication occurs
- Only PowerShell occurs
- The events occur on different hosts
- PowerShell occurs more than 600 seconds after the network logon

---

## Detection Engineering Lessons

### 1. Hunt Findings Require Engineering

HF-001 identified an interesting behavioral relationship, but the hunt query itself was not automatically suitable as a production analytic.

### 2. Fixed Time Buckets Can Create Boundary Problems

```spl
bin _time span=10m
```

was simple but did not represent true relative-time correlation.

### 3. Correlation Should Follow Event Order

The implemented analytic explicitly requires:

```text
Network Logon
BEFORE
PowerShell
```

### 4. Detection Opportunities Should Be Validated Before Promotion

DET-OPP-001 remained a candidate until:

- Correlation logic was developed
- Same-host correlation was implemented
- Relative-time logic was implemented
- Controlled positive validation succeeded

